  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#hasConcealedMaterialFact">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">May Commit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Indicates that an entity conceals a material fact that could affect the insurance contract. Assigned This property identifies concealed material facts, which are typically facts related to the insured or application. The…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Indicates that an entity conceals a material fact that could affect the insurance contract.</skos:definition>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">conceals</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">prevents fraud</skos:altLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#Policy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Policy</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A legal agreement between an insurer and a policyholder outlining coverage terms and conditions. Induced from a Placed as subClassOf ContractualAgreement (Stage 5, confidence: high); cluster of 6 surface variant(s) merge…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy must meet conditions to be reinstated after lapse. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Evidence shows reinstatement requires specific actions like providing evidence of insurability and paying past due prem…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy lapses if premium is not paid by due date. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The policy lapses when a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, directly linking non-payment to the lapse event; s…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Adjustments apply for inaccurate age or gender reporting. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; Evidence specifies that insurance amount is adjusted based on correct age or gender, indicating a direct relationship b…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Benefits are only available if contractual terms are met. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; All benefits are subject to contract terms and exclusions, indicating that eligibility depends on fulfilling defined co…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy cannot be contested after two years from issuance. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that the incontestability period begins after two years from the effective date, and this conditi…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Premium remains fixed at a guaranteed level throughout the term. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that premiums are guaranteed to remain level during the term, aligning with the concept of…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Prevents automatic premium loan activation under any circumstances. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states that the policy lacks an automatic premium loan provision, which implies a restriction on…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Coverage ends at term expiration unless conversion is elected. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that coverage termination occurs at term end unless conversion is elected, aligning with the…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policyholder is eligible for refund upon return within 20 days. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows refund eligibility is triggered by returning the policy within 20 days, directly linking the p…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Access to APL is permitted only via endorsement. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates that APL access is restricted to endorsement, supporting a someValuesFrom restriction. The low confidence…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy issuance requires a formal application. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence indicates policy issuance depends on a formal application. The property 'hasPolicyDefinition' is inferred as the clos…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Death benefit payout priority is determined by rules. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence shows distinct payout paths for beneficiaries, policy owners, and estates. The classes 'Beneficiary' and 'Poli…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Loans are deducted only after acceleration. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence states that outstanding loans and liens are deducted after acceleration. The property 'triggersLienDeductionAdjustment'…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Defines the components that constitute a policy. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The policy includes application, schedule, riders, and endorsements, suggesting a structural relationship. Although 'Policy' is…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Maximum amount payable under a policy is constrained. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence specifies a 50% cap on the accelerated death benefit, indicating a maximum limit. The cardinality is 1 because…</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Policy cancellation triggers coverage termination. Induced via Stage 6 restriction induction; The evidence confirms that cancellation directly causes coverage termination. The property 'terminates' correctly captures thi…</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A legal agreement between an insurer and a policyholder outlining coverage terms and conditions.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://example.org/ontology/insurance#ContractualAgreement"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ndcae406620c04f0ca4369450c9cee757b1"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="ndcae406620c04f0ca4369450c9cee757b4"/>
